note Translated from CPython Lib/_pydatetime.py datetime.replace (lines 2091 to 2114).
note Return a new datetime with new values for the specified fields.

type DateTime
    field year as an Int
    field month as an Int
    field day as an Int
    field hour as an Int
    field minute as an Int
    field second as an Int
    field microsecond as an Int
    field tzinfo as a maybe TimeZoneInfo
    field fold as an Int

note GAP: three-state argument - Python's tzinfo=True means "keep", None means "remove the zone", and a value means "set it"; maybe has only two states, so a choice is declared
choice TzinfoChange
    Keep
    Clear
    Set_to with zone as a TimeZoneInfo

to make_datetime year month day hour minute second microsecond tzinfo fold
    given year is an Int
    given month is an Int
    given day is an Int
    given hour is an Int
    given minute is an Int
    given second is an Int
    given microsecond is an Int
    given tzinfo is a maybe TimeZoneInfo
    given fold is an Int
    produces a DateTime
    fails with ValueError

note GAP: default and keyword arguments - every parameter defaults to None (or True for tzinfo) and fold is keyword-only, so callers write d.replace(day=1); the doc has neither defaults nor keywords, so every caller must pass nine values
note GAP: objects, methods and self - replace is a method; `type(self)(...)` builds an instance of the caller's subclass, and the doc has no self, no subclasses and no way to construct "the same type as this value"
to replace self year month day hour minute second microsecond tzinfo fold
    given self is a DateTime
    given year is a maybe Int
    given month is a maybe Int
    given day is a maybe Int
    given hour is a maybe Int
    given minute is a maybe Int
    given second is a maybe Int
    given microsecond is a maybe Int
    given tzinfo is a TzinfoChange
    given fold is a maybe Int
    produces a DateTime
    fails with ValueError

    note WORKAROUND: "if x is None, x = self.x" needs a choose per field, nine times; the doc has no "or else" default for a maybe outside a together block
    var new_year starts at year of self
    choose year
        when some y
            set new_year to y
        when nothing
            note keep year of self
    var new_month starts at month of self
    choose month
        when some m
            set new_month to m
        when nothing
            note keep month of self
    var new_day starts at day of self
    choose day
        when some d
            set new_day to d
        when nothing
            note keep day of self
    var new_hour starts at hour of self
    choose hour
        when some h
            set new_hour to h
        when nothing
            note keep hour of self
    var new_minute starts at minute of self
    choose minute
        when some m
            set new_minute to m
        when nothing
            note keep minute of self
    var new_second starts at second of self
    choose second
        when some s
            set new_second to s
        when nothing
            note keep second of self
    var new_microsecond starts at microsecond of self
    choose microsecond
        when some u
            set new_microsecond to u
        when nothing
            note keep microsecond of self
    var new_tzinfo starts at tzinfo of self
    choose tzinfo
        when Keep
            note keep tzinfo of self
        when Clear
            set new_tzinfo to nothing
        when Set_to with zone
            set new_tzinfo to some zone
    var new_fold starts at fold of self
    choose fold
        when some f
            set new_fold to f
        when nothing
            note keep fold of self
    note UNCLEAR: whether a when branch may hold only a note is not stated; the doc forbids an empty on failure line but says nothing about when
    give back try make_datetime new_year new_month new_day new_hour new_minute new_second new_microsecond new_tzinfo new_fold
